---
import { evidenceUrl, url } from "../lib/specs";
const milestones = [
  { status: "Verified on hardware", title: "The ESP SDR demo works", text: "The user-operated live viewer delivered 2,706 verified frames over 60 seconds. Two earlier minutes also passed. Each restored and verified the original 4 MiB firmware. The localhost viewer closes before restoration.", proof: "docs/evidence/esp-demo-play-001/README.md", label: "Interactive demo and restoration", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Fresh reception reproduced", title: "An owned BLE packet decoded", text: "Matched controls retained 1,994 valid snapshots. One fresh complete owned packet decoded at ten-bit/manual48; this does not establish a detection rate or a gain ranking.", proof: "docs/evidence/ble-matched-gain-001/README.md", label: "Fresh packet and waveform", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Controller-count condition verified", title: "100 controller events and cleanup verified", text: "The source and monitor agree on 100 completed extended-advertising events. Normal monitor completion and full cleanup pass. The earlier failed episode remains retained; auxiliary-channel AD supplies no legacy RF hit rate.", proof: "docs/evidence/ble-extended-count-limit-100-readiness-review/README.md", label: "Count, timing and cleanup review", kind: "partial" },
  { status: "Verified on hardware", title: "RTL-SDR delivers useful reception", text: "The attached dipole received FM/RDS identifying WXJC. The receiver comparison is accepted; calibrated shared-signal sensitivity remains deferred.", proof: "docs/evidence/rtl-dipole-rds/README.md", label: "Current-dipole RDS proof", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Identity-selected backend prepared", title: "Forgix gateware and its RP bridge build", text: "Both RAM bridge variants now advertise USB identity. Configuration bridge002 uses 203,152 SRAM bytes; register-only bridge010 uses 28,440. Twenty backend fault checks pass, alongside the configuration, collector and lifecycle checks. Host restoration is prepared. No FPGA was programmed. Hardware loading remains disabled: grade, clock, pin timing, independent backend review and production admission remain gates.", proof: "docs/evidence/forgix-spi-backend/README.md", label: "Backend checks, rebuilt images and limits", kind: "prepared" },
  { status: "64 KiB/s passes · 256 KiB/s loses data", title: "Forgix USB loss is measured", text: "The 64 KiB/s condition passes without loss. At requested 256 KiB/s, 15,530,520 payload bytes arrived over 60 seconds and 431 records were discarded, all accounted for. Full original-flash and factory verification passed. Maximum capacity and FPGA transport remain open.", proof: "docs/evidence/forgix-usb-ram-recovery/README.md", label: "USB measurements and retained failures", kind: "partial" },
];
---
<section class="project-checkpoint" aria-labelledby="checkpoint-title" data-project-checkpoint>
  <header><p class="eyebrow">CURRENT CHECKPOINT · OCTOBER 4, 2026</p><h2 id="checkpoint-title">The demo works. The next experiments have clear gates.</h2><p>Hardware results, software preparation and failed experiments are shown separately. The full RF and FPGA evaluations remain open.</p></header>
  <div class="milestones">{milestones.map(item => <article class={`milestone ${item.kind}`}><span class="milestone-status">{item.status}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p><a href={evidenceUrl(item.proof)}>{item.label} →</a></article>)}</div>
  <div class="next-work"><div><p class="eyebrow">NEXT, IN ORDER</p><ol><li><strong>Prepare FPGA register readback.</strong> Qualify board parameters and pin timing, then independently review the prepared identity-selected backend and add production admission using its rebuilt configuration variant, tested lifecycle controller and private collector. Verify physical configuration and register readback. Earlier full preservation passes; refresh it before loading; physical FPGA transport is untested.</li><li><strong>Advance controlled ESP reception.</strong> Prepare the required eight-bit/BW12/hardware-gain positive control with reviewed monitor clocks. The passing source-only count condition supplies no legacy reception denominator.</li><li><strong>Diagnose USB stalls and buffering.</strong> Use retained queue and loss timing before declaring another condition. The 256 KiB/s loss does not establish a USB ceiling; measure the complete FPGA route before RF integration.</li></ol></div><aside><h3>What we need from you</h3><p>Forgix was reconnected and earlier fresh original-flash/factory verification passed after the retained timeout. Leave it connected; no ESP wiring or RF equipment is needed for the first register test. Your photos are received and your S31 remains backordered. The small FPGA chip’s T8F49 suffix is still unreadable in the received photos; grade and actual clock need qualification.</p><h3>Will Forgix need wires to the ESP?</h3><p>The proposed direct path needs verified SPI I/O and a common ground. Forgix keeps USB to the PC. A PC-mediated processing demo is another option, but keeps ESP capture gaps. No inter-board wiring is needed for the current USB test.</p><a href={url("fpga/")}>Transport stages and pin ownership →</a></aside></div>
</section>
<style>
  .project-checkpoint { margin:2.5rem 0; padding:1.6rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface); color:var(--ink); }
  header { max-width:64rem; margin-bottom:1.4rem; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.7vw,2.2rem); line-height:1.15; margin:.5rem 0 .8rem; }
  header p, article p, aside p, li { color:var(--ink-2); line-height:1.55; }
  .milestones { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1rem; }
  .milestone { padding:1.1rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-top:3px solid var(--accent); border-radius:7px; }
  .partial { border-top-color:var(--unverified); }
  .prepared { border-top-color:var(--muted); }
  .milestone-status { font: .65rem var(--mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.05em; color:var(--muted); }
  h3 { font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.25; margin:.65rem 0; }
  article p { font-size:.9rem; margin:.7rem 0 1rem; }
  a { color:var(--accent); font-size:.88rem; }
  .next-work { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.45fr 1fr; gap:2rem; margin-top:1.5rem; padding-top:1.4rem; border-top:1px solid var(--rule); }
  ol { padding-left:1.2rem; margin:.7rem 0 0; }
  li { margin:.65rem 0; font-size:.92rem; }
  aside { padding:1rem 1.2rem; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:7px; }
  aside h3:first-child { margin-top:0; }
  aside p { font-size:.9rem; }
  @media(max-width:1050px) { .milestones { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); } }
  @media(max-width:650px) { .project-checkpoint { padding:1rem; } .milestones,.next-work { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .next-work { gap:1rem; } }
</style>
